<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!--
        carddemo-adapter-file — DEFAULT outer-ring repository adapter of the
        hexagonal architecture (AAP §0.3.6).

        Contents (AAP §0.2.1, §0.3.1):
          * FixedWidthReader / FixedWidthWriter — byte-for-byte fixed-width
            record I/O via java.nio.file (Files.newByteChannel,
            SeekableByteChannel, Files.write, Files.readAllBytes); java.io.File
            is forbidden per AAP §0.6.5.
          * EbcdicTranscoder — Charset.forName("IBM-1047") default with
            per-file codepage overrides via application.properties
            (carddemo.file.&lt;dataset&gt;.charset=...) per AAP §0.6.5.
          * One File*Repository implementation per port interface declared in
            carddemo-domain.port (AccountRepository, CardRepository,
            CardXrefRepository, CustomerRepository, TransactionRepository,
            DailyTransactionRepository, DiscountGroupRepository,
            TransactionCategoryBalanceRepository, TransactionTypeRepository,
            TransactionCategoryRepository, UserSecurityRepository — AAP §0.3.1).

        Why this is the production-default adapter (AAP §0.1.1, §0.7.5):
          The COBOL source uses VSAM KSDS and sequential files with fixed-width
          records — the default migration target is java.nio.file with
          fixed-width readers, NOT a relational database. The alternate
          adapter (carddemo-adapter-db) is empty by default; this module is
          wired by the composition root (carddemo-app) at startup.

        Architectural rule (AAP §0.3.6, §0.6.12):
          * This module depends ONLY on carddemo-domain (innermost ring).
          * This module is depended on by carddemo-app (composition root) and
            indirectly by carddemo-tests — never the reverse.
          * Outer rings of the hexagon must not be coupled to each other, so
            this module must NOT depend on carddemo-application,
            carddemo-batch, carddemo-adapter-db, carddemo-app, or
            carddemo-tests.

        Forbidden here (AAP §0.1.1 architectural override, §0.5.1, §0.6.5,
        §0.6.7, §0.6.12, §0.7.4):
          * Spring / Spring Boot / Spring Data / Spring Batch / Spring
            Security / Spring MVC / Spring Cloud AWS — plain Java with
            java.nio.file only. No org.springframework.* dependencies (notably
            no spring-core: do not use Spring's Resource abstraction; use
            java.nio.file.Path exclusively).
          * Hibernate / JPA / jakarta.persistence / javax.persistence
          * Lombok — Java 25 records replace it (AAP §0.7.3).
          * Apache Commons IO — java.nio.file covers all needs per AAP §0.5.1.
          * Guava — java.nio.file and java.util collections cover all needs.
          * JDBC drivers (PostgreSQL, MySQL, DB2, H2) — those belong to the
            optional carddemo-adapter-db module, NOT here.
          * Flyway, Liquibase, Testcontainers, LocalStack
          * Micrometer, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry, Jaeger
          * jqwik (property tests live in carddemo-tests per AAP §0.3.1).
          * The "enable-preview" JVM flag (AAP §0.7.4 — finalized JEPs only:
            JEP 506 ScopedValue, JEP 510 KDF, JEP 511 Module Import, JEP 513
            Flexible Constructor Bodies, JEP 519 Compact Headers, JEP 521
            Generational Shenandoah).
          * &lt;source&gt;/&lt;target&gt; tags — the parent POM's
            &lt;release&gt;25&lt;/release&gt; is the single source of truth for
            the Java language level.
    -->

    <parent>
        <groupId>com.blitzy.carddemo</groupId>
        <artifactId>carddemo-parent</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>carddemo-adapter-file</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>CardDemo Adapter (File)</name>
    <description>
        File-backed repository adapter implementing every port interface from
        carddemo-domain.port via java.nio.file. Fixed-width record readers and
        writers preserve byte-for-byte fidelity to COBOL VSAM/sequential file
        output (AAP §0.6.5). EBCDIC IBM-1047 default codepage with per-file
        overrides via application.properties. DEFAULT outer-ring adapter
        (carddemo-adapter-db is empty by default per AAP §0.7.5). NO Spring,
        NO frameworks, NO java.io.File. Depends only on carddemo-domain.
    </description>

    <dependencies>
        <!--
            Internal dependency: carddemo-domain.
            Provides:
              * Repository port interfaces (AccountRepository, CardRepository,
                CardXrefRepository, CustomerRepository, TransactionRepository,
                DailyTransactionRepository, DiscountGroupRepository,
                TransactionCategoryBalanceRepository, TransactionTypeRepository,
                TransactionCategoryRepository, UserSecurityRepository — AAP §0.3.1)
                that every File*Repository in this module implements.
              * Java records translated from COBOL copybook 01-level groups
                (AccountRecord, CardRecord, CardXrefRecord, CustomerRecord,
                TranRecord, DalyTranRecord, TranCatBalRecord, DisGroupRecord,
                TranTypeRecord, TranCatRecord, SecUserData, TrnxRecord,
                CardDemoCommarea, CustomerLegacyRecord, ReportHeaders,
                UnusedRecord — AAP §0.4.1, §0.6.9) that the FixedWidthReader
                and FixedWidthWriter parse/encode.
              * Decimals utility — BigDecimal facade with MathContext.DECIMAL128
                and explicit RoundingMode selection (HALF_EVEN for ROUNDED,
                DOWN otherwise) used during signed-packed-decimal encode/decode
                in the FixedWidth reader/writer (AAP §0.3.3, §0.6.1).
              * Sealed FileStatus hierarchy (Ok, EndOfFile, NotFound,
                DuplicateKey, IoError) — translation target for COBOL FILE
                STATUS codes; each File*Repository raises typed instances of
                this hierarchy with identical observable outcomes per AAP §0.6.10.
              * @CobolProgram traceability annotation cited in Javadoc on every
                File*Repository to record the original PROGRAM-ID and source
                file path (AAP §0.2.1, §0.7.1).
            Version inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement
            (${project.version} = 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT).
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.blitzy.carddemo</groupId>
            <artifactId>carddemo-domain</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!--
            Production dependency: SLF4J API only (compile scope).
            Used by:
              * FileAccountRepository, FileCardRepository, FileCustomerRepository,
                FileTransactionRepository, FileDailyTransactionRepository, and
                every other File*Repository in this module — to log file open
                and close events, fixed-width record read/write counts, and
                FILE STATUS code translations to the FileStatus sealed
                hierarchy.
              * FixedWidthReader / FixedWidthWriter — to log buffer underrun,
                truncation, and sign-nybble anomalies during signed packed
                decimal parse/encode.
              * EbcdicTranscoder — to log IBM-1047 transcoding warnings (e.g.,
                non-roundtrip codepoints) and per-file codepage override
                application per AAP §0.6.5.
            The runtime implementation (logback-classic) is supplied by the
            composition root (carddemo-app); this adapter depends only on the
            API, keeping it free of binding to a specific logging backend per
            AAP §0.6.12.
            Version is inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement
            (slf4j-api 2.0.16 per AAP §0.5.1).
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!--
            Test dependencies (test scope only).
            Versions are inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement:
              * junit-jupiter            via junit-bom 5.13.1 (AAP §0.5.1) —
                                                  unit tests for byte-for-byte
                                                  parse/encode round-trips on
                                                  FixedWidthReader and
                                                  FixedWidthWriter, EBCDIC
                                                  IBM-1047 transcoding
                                                  correctness, and File*Repository
                                                  contract conformance against
                                                  in-memory and tempfile-backed
                                                  fixtures.
              * junit-platform-launcher  1.13.1 — required minimum for JUnit
                                                  Platform native discovery by
                                                  maven-surefire-plugin 3.5.2
                                                  and aligns with jqwik 1.9.3's
                                                  minimum platform requirement
                                                  used by carddemo-tests
                                                  (AAP §0.5.1).
              * assertj-core 3.27.7 — fluent assertions used to
                                                  express expectations such as
                                                  assertThat(actualBytes)
                                                  .isEqualTo(expectedBytes)
                                                  for byte-level fidelity and
                                                  FileStatus pattern-match
                                                  assertions (AAP §0.5.1).
            Note: jqwik is NOT declared here — property-based tests for the
            Decimals utility and any cross-module property tests live in
            carddemo-tests per AAP §0.3.1.
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.platform</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-platform-launcher</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.assertj</groupId>
            <artifactId>assertj-core</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!--
                maven-compiler-plugin — activated for this module so the
                parent's pluginManagement (version 3.13.0,
                &lt;release&gt;25&lt;/release&gt;, no preview flag per AAP
                §0.7.4, -parameters for record component names) applies during
                the compile phase. The Java language level is set ONCE in the
                parent POM; this child must not redeclare it.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                maven-surefire-plugin — activated for this module so the
                parent's pluginManagement (version 3.5.2, JUnit Platform
                native discovery, no "enable-preview" argLine per AAP §0.7.4)
                applies during the test phase. Test classes are discovered by
                the standard **/*Test.java and **/*Tests.java patterns.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
